{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_014okMYtGqqzqFsH9GKXTa2o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"For the Great Hall, the test will need to test:\n1. {T}: Add {C}\n2. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color (restricted to instant/sorcery)\n3. {5}: Become a 2/4 Wizard creature (still a land) with pump trigger\n\nFor the mana abilities, the key pattern from basic_lands.py is:\n- `cost` function: `(game, source) -> bool` - check and pay\n- `mana_produced` function: `(game) -> None` - add mana to pool\n\nThe {T} cost checks if the source is untapped, then taps it. For the life payment cost, I need to verify the source isn't tapped and the player has at least 2 life remaining before tapping and paying 1 life. The restricted mana ability requires adding a lightweight marker to track that the mana can only be used for instant or sorcery spells.\n\nThe tricky part is that `ManaPool` currently just stores a count by type, so I need to add a separate counter for restricted colorless mana. When the life payment ability triggers, it increments this restricted counter, and then during payment, I check the spell type before using restricted mana. The issue is that `can_pay` only receives a `ManaCost`, not information about the spell's type, so I need to thread that context through the payment flow. I could add an optional flag to both `can_pay` and `pay` methods to indicate whether we're paying for an instant or sorcery, then adjust the available mana calculation accordingly—restricting non-instant/sorcery spells from using the reserved mana pool. Adding mana pool methods... I'm thinking about separating restricted colorless mana into its own pool so I can track it independently. When checking if I can pay a cost, I'd include restricted mana only if it's allowed for that spell type. During payment, if restricted mana gets used, I'd decrement that separate pool. But this is getting complicated, so I'm considering an even simpler approach with just an `add_restricted` method. Adding the restriction tracking...\n\nThe key insight from the context is that I need to enforce this at payment time in `cast_spell`, not during `can_pay`. So I'll track restricted mana in the pool and when paying for a spell, if it's not an instant or sorcery, I exclude that restricted mana from being available. I'm realizing the interface approach is getting messy, so I need a cleaner way to handle this. The real issue is that `can_pay` doesn't know what type of spell is being cast, so I need the caller to pass that information along when checking if restricted colorless should be excluded from the available pool.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":205,"cache_read_input_tokens":148546,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":205},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"78db596a-d666-492a-a333-89a7fe9e7ac5","request_id":"req_011CbwGXE93x3MBwA8usorhp"}
