{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked the `execute-todo` skill to implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace`. The skill instruction requires reading `/workspace/TODO.md` and `/workspace/CONTEXT.md`, then implementing all cards in the checklist in order through the real engine, running engine_tests after each, and never stopping to ask questions. This is an unattended single-shot run targeting cards: sos_1, sos_4, sos_13, sos_57, sos_97, sos_120, sos_201, sos_226, sos_245, sos_257.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Magic: The Gathering card implementation in Python OOP\n   - Engine extension points: cost_reduction hooks, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities, get_mana_abilities, get_loyalty_abilities\n   - Triggered abilities via TriggerManager.register(TriggerRegistration(...))\n   - Replacement effects via ReplacementManager.register(ReplacementEffect(...))\n   - SpellCastTriggeredEvent (E1) - fires when spells are cast\n   - BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent (E2) - fires at start of precombat main\n   - Battlefield cost reduction aggregation (E3) - spell_cost_reduction(game, card) hook on permanents\n   - Free-cast from zones via cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)\n   - Spell copy via copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)\n   - Zone transitions via move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, replacement_event)\n   - MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent for exile-instead effects\n   - AttacksTriggeredEvent firing in declare_attackers_step\n   - Restricted mana: ManaPool._restricted_colorless with allow_restricted parameter\n   - DeterministicPlayer: script-driven choices for tests\n   - TargetRequirement: filter_fn + description + zone\n   - ManaCost: generic + pips + hybrid\n   - CardType: INSTANT, SORCERY, CREATURE, LAND, PLANESWALKER, etc.\n   - Keyword: bitflags for REACH, FLYING, DEATHTOUCH, VIGILANCE, HASTE, etc.\n   - Zone: BATTLEFIELD, HAND, GRAVEYARD, EXILE, STACK, LIBRARY\n   - Converge: X = number of distinct colors of mana spent (from card.colors_spent)\n   - Affinity: cost_reduction + spell_cost_reduction hooks\n   - Casualty 1: sacrifice creature power ≥ 1 to copy spell\n   - Additive-only engine rule: never rename/move/delete existing engine symbols\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/TODO.md` - Implementation plan with ordered checklist. Now has E1, E2, E3, sos_4, sos_1, sos_245, sos_226 marked [x].\n   - `/workspace/CONTEXT.md` - Glossary of MTG mechanics (Converge, Affinity, Miracle, Casualty, Prepared, Paradigm, Surveil)\n   - `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` - Created to track implementation decisions\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` - Added `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` (fieldless dataclass):\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n         pass\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` - Multiple changes:\n     1. E1: Fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent in cast_spell after stack.push:\n        ```python\n        from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, card=card, controller=player))\n        ```\n     2. E1: Same in cast_spell_free\n     3. E3: Extended get_cost_reduction to aggregate battlefield permanents:\n        ```python\n        if CardType.INSTANT in card.card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card.card_types:\n            bf = game.get_battlefield(controller)\n            for permanent in bf.get_all():\n                reducer = getattr(permanent, \"spell_cost_reduction\", None)\n                if callable(reducer):\n                    raw += reducer(game, card)\n        ```\n     4. _resolve_spell: Apply MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent for Stack→Graveyard:\n        ```python\n        from engine.events import MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent\n        owner = getattr(card, \"owner\", player)\n        repl_event = MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination=\"graveyard\", controller=player, owner=owner)\n        repl_event._source_card = card\n        repl_event = game.replacement_manager.apply(game, repl_event)\n        if not getattr(repl_event, \"prevented\", False):\n            dest_str = getattr(repl_event, \"destination\", \"graveyard\")\n            dest = {\"graveyard\": Zone.GRAVEYARD, \"exile\": Zone.EXILE, ...}.get(dest_str, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n            move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, dest)\n        ```\n     5. In cast_spell, pass allow_restricted to can_pay/pay:\n        ```python\n        _is_inst_or_sorc = bool(card.card_types & {CardType.INSTANT, CardType.SORCERY})\n        if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(effective_cost, allow_restricted=_is_inst_or_sorc): ...\n        player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost, allow_restricted=_is_inst_or_sorc)\n        ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` - E2: Fire event after empty_mana_pools in advance_phase:\n     ```python\n     if self.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN:\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent\n         self.trigger_manager.fire_event(self, BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent())\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` - Fire AttacksTriggeredEvent per attacker in declare_attackers_step:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py` - Added restricted mana support:\n     - `_restricted_colorless: int = 0` attribute in `__init__`\n     - `empty()` also resets `_restricted_colorless = 0`\n     - `add_restricted(mana_type, amount)` method\n     - `can_pay(cost, *, allow_restricted=True)` - excludes restricted colorless when False\n     - `pay(cost, choices=None, *, allow_restricted=True)` - works on restricted pool\n     - Updates `_restricted_colorless` after payment (decrements by consumed colorless)\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` - Together as One (Sorcery, Converge):\n     ```python\n     class TogetherAsOne(Sorcery):\n         def get_targets(self, game): # 2 targets: player + any target\n         def on_resolve(self, game):\n             colors_spent = getattr(self, \"colors_spent\", [])\n             x = len(set(colors_spent))\n             # draw x, deal x damage, gain x life\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` - 6 tests, all passing\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` - The Dawning Archaic (Creature):\n     ```python\n     class TheDawningArchaic(Creature):\n         def cost_reduction(self, game): # count inst/sorc in graveyard\n         def register_triggers(self, game): # AttacksTriggeredEvent → choose inst/sorc from GY → cast_spell_free + register exile replacement\n     def _register_exile_replacement(game, spell, controller):\n         def _condition(game, event): return getattr(event, \"_source_card\", None) is spell\n         def _replacement(game, event):\n             event.destination = \"exile\"\n             game.replacement_manager.unregister(spell)\n             return event\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` - 10 tests, all passing (includes manual `archaic.register_triggers(game)` call since set_board_state doesn't call it)\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` - Witherbloom, the Balancer:\n     ```python\n     class WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature):\n         def cost_reduction(self, game): # affinity: count creatures you control\n         def spell_cost_reduction(self, game, spell): # E3 hook: grant affinity to controller's instants/sorceries\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` - 8 tests, all passing\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` - Silverquill, the Disputant:\n     ```python\n     class SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature):\n         def register_triggers(self, game):\n             # SpellCastTriggeredEvent: if controller casts inst/sorc\n             # → choose_card for creature with power ≥ 1 (or None to decline)\n             # → sacrifice creature → copy_spell → push copy to stack\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` - 7 tests, all passing\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` - Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land):\n     ```python\n     class GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land):\n         def get_mana_abilities(self): # {T}→{C} and {T}+1life→restricted colored\n         def get_activated_abilities(self): # {5}: animate as 2/4 Wizard, register pump trigger\n     def _register_pump_trigger(game, source):\n         # SpellCastTriggeredEvent → +1/+0 modified_power\n         # EndStepTriggeredEvent → reset to base 2\n     ```\n     Note: Tests not yet written or run for sos_257.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **AttacksTriggeredEvent never fired in engine**: Defined in events.py but `declare_attackers_step` never fired it. Found by debugging: `game.stack._items` was empty after `declare_attackers`. Fixed by adding `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))` in `combat.py`.\n   - **set_board_state doesn't register triggers**: When placing the Dawning Archaic on battlefield via set_board_state, `register_triggers` is never called (set_board_state bypasses move_to_zone). Fixed by calling `archaic.register_triggers(game)` manually in tests after set_board_state.\n   - **MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent not applied for Stack→Graveyard**: move_to_zone only applied replacement effects when `from_zone == Zone.BATTLEFIELD`. For non-permanent spells resolving (Stack→Graveyard), replacements were skipped. Fixed by adding explicit replacement event handling in `_resolve_spell` with `_source_card` attribute to identify the specific card.\n   - **Replacement condition too broad**: Initial implementation used `event.owner is getattr(spell, \"owner\", None)` which would match ANY spell from that player. Fixed to use `getattr(event, \"_source_card\", None) is spell` after adding `_source_card` to the replacement event.\n   - **sos_4 target filter**: The \"target player\" filter used `hasattr(obj, \"life\") and hasattr(obj, \"zones\")` to distinguish players from creatures (creatures don't have `zones`).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Exile-instead for spells resolving**: MTG replacement effects (MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent) are only applied in move_to_zone when `leaving_battlefield`. For sos_1's \"exile instead\" mechanic when spell resolves from stack, extended `_resolve_spell` to create and apply a MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent, attaching `_source_card` to identify the specific spell.\n   - **Restricted mana for sos_257**: The spec requires mana from the land's second ability can \"only be spent to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\" Added `_restricted_colorless` tracking to ManaPool and `allow_restricted` parameter to `can_pay`/`pay`. The `cast_spell` function passes `allow_restricted=False` for non-instant/sorcery spells to prevent restricted mana from being used.\n   - **E3 aggregation**: `get_cost_reduction` now queries `spell_cost_reduction(game, card)` from each permanent on the caster's battlefield when the spell is instant or sorcery.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Run the `execute-todo` skill now to implement the SOS cards. Your task and prepared execution plan are in /workspace/TODO.md and /workspace/CONTEXT.md.\"\n   - (Skill invocation result text from the execute-todo skill with detailed instructions about the implementation loop)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Complete sos_257 (Great Hall of the Biblioplex): Write and run tests\n   - Implement sos_57 (Mana Sculpt): counter spell + delayed {C} mana if you control a Wizard, uses E2\n   - Implement sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone): exile top cards until MV≥4, cast free; Paradigm mechanic, uses E2\n   - Implement sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares): ETB token, prepared mechanic, SwordsToPlowshares helper\n   - Implement sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian): Flying/Haste, miracle {2} for hand instants/sorceries, loot on opponent's upkeep\n   - Implement sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer): Planeswalker with Surveil 2, discard, reanimate, coin flip + skip turns\n   - Run final `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` verification\n   - Commit all uncommitted changes\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I had just finished writing `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` (Great Hall of the Biblioplex implementation). The file was written but tests have NOT been written or run yet. I also modified `/workspace/engine/mana.py` to support restricted mana (`_restricted_colorless`, `add_restricted()`, `allow_restricted` params) and updated `engine/casting.py` to pass `allow_restricted` based on spell type. The engine tests all pass (1145 passed).\n\n   The last text in the conversation was: \"Let me look at how activated abilities work in the engine:\" and a search for `ActivateAbility` - which found it's only mentioned in TODO.md as documentation guidance (not an actual class). This means tests for sos_257 should directly test the mana abilities by calling the effect callbacks or using the `activate_ability` function from `engine/abilities.py` with `ActivatedAbilityInstance`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue implementing sos_257 by writing and running tests for Great Hall of the Biblioplex. The card implementation is in place at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py`. Need to:\n   1. Write `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` testing the three abilities ({T}→{C}, {T}+life→restricted mana, {5}→animate)\n   2. Run tests and fix any issues\n   3. Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` to verify no regressions\n   4. Mark `sos_257` done in TODO.md and commit\n   5. Then continue with sos_57\n\n   Direct quote from TODO.md showing current position:\n   \"- [ ] **sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex** *(uses E1; land: mana + restriction + animation)*\"\n   And from the skill instructions: \"For each incomplete `- [ ]` item: 1. Read the spec... 5. Test through the real engine. Write 2–5 focused tests... 7. Guard the engine. Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q`. 8. Mark `- [x]` in `TODO.md` and commit... 9. Move to the next item.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"b22eb9b2-4073-4149-a293-a42f32abdf12","timestamp":"2026-06-11T09:58:44.720Z","isSynthetic":true}
