{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01MLPXZSS6YL6eUbkUhvhPsU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand how to drive choices. For the second mana ability, `choose(colors, \"Choose a color...\")` will pop from the script. So I script the color.\n\nNow let me write the tests file. I want:\n\n1. `test_colorless_mana_ability` - {T}: Add {C}, verify pool has 1 colorless\n2. `test_life_payment_adds_colored_restricted_mana` - {T}, Pay 1 life, script a color, verify pool and life changed\n3. `test_life_payment_fails_if_one_life_remaining` - can't pay if life <= 1\n4. `test_animate_becomes_creature` - after {5}, card_types includes CREATURE, 2/4 stats, Wizard subtype\n5. `test_pump_trigger_on_instant_cast` - after animation, cast instant, check modified_power increased\n\nI'll use `ActivatedAbilityInstance` and `activate_ability` directly like in test_abilities.py. For the animation test, I need to set up 5 mana in the pool, then for the pump trigger test, I'll set up the Hall on the battlefield, add the mana, and trigger the instant cast to verify the power boost. I need to understand how `fire_event` actually works in the trigger system to see whether triggers get pushed to the stack or fire immediately when an event occurs.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":59525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":678},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"65793ef4-35d7-43b5-9694-cff049801dd1","request_id":"req_011CbwH45sqPww6ixqginM7y"}
