{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01F22YrxTZpkpkgzZURRMp2N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now understand the pattern. Let me implement sos_57 — Mana Sculpt.\n\nThe card:\n- Cost: {1}{U}{U}\n- Counter target spell\n- If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\n\nKey implementation points:\n1. Counter the spell (same as Refute's `_counter_spell`)\n2. Track the amount of mana spent to cast the countered spell (mana spent = cost after reductions, actually paid)\n3. Check if you control a Wizard after countering\n4. If so, register a one-shot trigger on the beginning of my next precombat main phase that adds colorless mana equal to what was paid\n5. For \"mana spent,\" I need to capture the total mana value actually paid when the spell was cast — that's the sum of all the pips in the effective cost plus any generic mana\n\nThe tricky part is distinguishing between the spell's printed mana cost and what was actually spent after reductions or discounts. In MTG rules, \"mana spent\" technically refers to the actual amount paid, but for practical purposes here I should use the mana value of the countered spell.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1558,"cache_read_input_tokens":68208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1558},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"8c449452-9599-4789-991b-2ea286b13e5e","request_id":"req_011CbwHAowpk2mftdjj6YC7s"}
