{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0125x7B5DHbpVV2Gm7eE5kSE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `ManaCost.cmc` gives the converted mana cost. The \"mana spent\" for the countered spell is the mana value/CMC of the original spell (since in MTG, \"mana spent to cast\" refers to the total mana spent, which in the context of countering generally means the spell's CMC minus any reductions, but we can approximate with the spell's printed mana cost CMC).\n\nActually, re-reading: \"add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\" - this means the actual mana the opponent paid. \n\nThe problem is that once mana gets paid through the pool, there's no record of what was actually spent on a particular spell. The most practical approach is to use the mana value of the countered spell, which is what most MTG engines do. I should check if the StackObject has any cost tracking that might help me get the actual mana spent rather than just the CMC.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":398,"cache_read_input_tokens":70640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":398},"output_tokens":47,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"4f49a9bd-88e8-4484-8721-d832b66edead","request_id":"req_011CbwHCNvjLH8kP5BD9tEK6"}
