{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011ZxBW9zsFKiVG5Se2EBb3E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`StackObject` doesn't track how much mana was paid for the spell. The simplest approach is to use the spell's mana value (CMC) from `source.mana_cost.cmc` on the countered spell. Let me log this as a deliberate decision.\n\nNow let me implement sos_57:\n\nThe implementation:\n1. Copy `_counter_spell` from fdn_48 (or import it... actually no, it's not exported. I'll copy/reference it)\n2. In `on_resolve`:\n   - Get the countered spell's CMC (as \"mana spent\")\n   - Counter the spell via `_counter_spell`\n   - Check if the controller has a Wizard on the battlefield\n   - If so, set up a one-shot trigger for the beginning of their next precombat main phase that adds mana equal to the spell's CMC, then unregisters itself\n\nThe trigger needs to verify it's actually the controller's main phase and fire only once before cleaning up.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":725,"cache_read_input_tokens":71420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":725},"output_tokens":39,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"be4dbae1-6e58-482c-a43f-560e2e31bbdc","request_id":"req_011CbwHDGGAUwsuwysPx7ZoL"}
