{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01PqGRpxAgFk8WUSxz5yMKgF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me understand the full spec:\n1. Exile cards from top of library until total mana value >= 4\n2. You may cast any number of them for free (without paying mana costs)\n3. **Paradigm**: After resolving, exile this spell (instead of graveyard). Then at the beginning of each of your first main phases (precombat main), you may cast a copy of it from exile for free.\n\nThe Paradigm mechanic:\n- When the Capstone resolves for the first time, it gets exiled instead of going to the graveyard\n- Each precombat main phase, I can cast a copy from exile for free, which triggers the same exile-and-cast effect again\n- But the copy itself doesn't re-trigger Paradigm since it's not the original spell—the Paradigm trigger was already established on the first resolution\n- Copies of spells that would go to the graveyard just go to the graveyard normally, so the copy doesn't get exiled again like the original does\n- Now I'm thinking through the implementation: the sorcery needs to handle the initial resolution with the exile effect and the recurring trigger for each precombat main phase\n\n, but only on the first cast, not on copies\n- I need to figure out how to distinguish between the original spell and its copies—maybe by checking if this is the canonical instance or using a flag to track whether the Paradigm trigger has already been registered","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":706,"cache_read_input_tokens":82553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":706},"output_tokens":37,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"c3979a