{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_014QwoPoDR9sXByQknyjpTNz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `_resolve_spell`:\n1. Calls `card.on_resolve(game)` first\n2. Then checks if it's a permanent → move to battlefield\n3. Otherwise → apply replacement effects, then move to graveyard/exile\n\nFor Paradigm, I need the card to go to EXILE instead of graveyard. I can use the replacement effect mechanism via `register_replacement_effects` or I can handle it directly in `on_resolve` by registering a one-time replacement effect.\n\nBut actually, looking at how sos_1's exile-instead works (from the summary), I already have the pattern: register a `ReplacementEffect` with `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` that sets `destination = \"exile\"` and identifies the specific card via `_source_card`.\n \nThe cleanest approach is to set up a replacement effect inside `on_resolve` that intercepts the zone move to graveyard and redirects it to exile instead. This same replacement effect can also trigger the Paradigm setup, so everything happens in one place. Since `on_resolve` runs before the zone move happens, I can register the effect there and it'll catch the move. Let me check how sos_1 handles this pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_read_input_tokens":87408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954},"output_tokens":37,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"5bb22a58-72f6-4e21-985b-392fbd1b312e","request_id":"req_011CbwHV7rb7uemQBujce1Ao"}
