{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01358mMx5c1ctqpHjkKMg1pk","type":"tool_result","content":"273\tdef cast_spell_free(\n274\t    game: GameState,\n275\t    player: Player,\n276\t    card: CardImpl,\n277\t    from_zone: Zone,\n278\t) -> None:\n279\t    \"\"\"Cast *card* without paying its mana cost, using the stack.\n280\t\n281\t    This is used by effects that allow casting from zones other than hand\n282\t    (e.g. exile) without paying mana costs — such as Etali, Primal Storm\n283\t    or cascade.\n284\t\n285\t    Pipeline\n286\t    --------\n287\t    1. **can_cast** — ask the card whether it can legally be cast (same\n288\t       legality as :func:`cast_spell`, minus mana/timing constraints).\n289\t    2. Move *card* from *from_zone* to the stack zone.\n290\t    3. Choose targets (if applicable) with validation and protection check.\n291\t    4. Call ``on_cast`` hook.\n292\t    5. Push a :class:`StackObject` whose ``on_resolve`` callback handles\n293\t       resolution normally (permanents → battlefield, non-permanents →\n294\t       graveyard).\n295\t\n296\t    No timing check or mana payment is performed.  The spell goes on the\n297\t    stack and can be responded to normally (e.g. countered).\n298\t\n299\t    If targeting or other post-move checks fail, the card is rolled back\n300\t    to its source zone.\n301\t\n302\t    Parameters:\n303\t        game: The current game state.\n304\t        player: The player casting the spell.\n305\t        card: The card to cast.\n306\t        from_zone: The zone the card is currently in.\n307\t\n308\t    Raises:\n309\t        CastingError: If the card cannot be found in *from_zone* or\n310\t            legality checks fail.\n311\t    \"\"\"\n312\t    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n313\t\n314\t    # Ensure controller is set\n315\t    card.controller = player\n316\t    if card.owner is None:\n317\t        card.owner = player\n318\t\n319\t    # 1. can_cast legality (same as cast_spell but skipping mana/timing)\n320\t    if not card.can_cast(game):\n321\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n322\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"91464ddc-ee07-4e0c-8004-5aa392e5542b","timestamp":"2026-06-11T10:06:10.467Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/engine/casting.py","content":"def cast_spell_free(\n    game: GameState,\n    player: Player,\n    card: CardImpl,\n    from_zone: Zone,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Cast *card* without paying its mana cost, using the stack.\n\n    This is used by effects that allow casting from zones other than hand\n    (e.g. exile) without paying mana costs — such as Etali, Primal Storm\n    or cascade.\n\n    Pipeline\n    --------\n    1. **can_cast** — ask the card whether it can legally be cast (same\n       legality as :func:`cast_spell`, minus mana/timing constraints).\n    2. Move *card* from *from_zone* to the stack zone.\n    3. Choose targets (if applicable) with validation and protection check.\n    4. Call ``on_cast`` hook.\n    5. Push a :class:`StackObject` whose ``on_resolve`` callback handles\n       resolution normally (permanents → battlefield, non-permanents →\n       graveyard).\n\n    No timing check or mana payment is performed.  The spell goes on the\n    stack and can be responded to normally (e.g. countered).\n\n    If targeting or other post-move checks fail, the card is rolled back\n    to its source zone.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        player: The player casting the spell.\n        card: The card to cast.\n        from_zone: The zone the card is currently in.\n\n    Raises:\n        CastingError: If the card cannot be found in *from_zone* or\n            legality checks fail.\n    \"\"\"\n    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n\n    # Ensure controller is set\n    card.controller = player\n    if card.owner is None:\n        card.owner = player\n\n    # 1. can_cast legality (same as cast_spell but skipping mana/timing)\n    if not card.can_cast(game):\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n","numLines":50,"startLine":273,"totalLines":538}}}
