{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01E7EDP6Kcc5nnHD7XfsYT8D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to put the card in the exile zone before calling `cast_spell_free`. So the Paradigm trigger will:\n1. Create a copy of the original exiled card: `import copy; cap_copy = copy.copy(self)` where `self` is the exiled Capstone\n2. Set it up with `_is_paradigm_copy = True`\n3. Place it in the exile zone: `exile_zone.add(cap_copy)`\n4. Call `cast_spell_free(game, controller, cap_copy, Zone.EXILE)` - this moves it from exile to stack\nSince the original Capstone is already in exile, I can't just cast it repeatedly—each cast moves it to the stack and eventually to the graveyard, so I need to create a fresh copy in exile each time to cast from there.\n\nI'm setting up a pattern where I create a shallow copy of the original card, mark it with a flag to distinguish it as a Paradigm copy, assign the proper controller and owner, add it to the exile zone, and then cast it for free. The copy will resolve and go to the graveyard afterward, while the original stays safely in exile. I'll use that flag to check whether this is the first resolution (where I exile and cast from library) or a subsequent copy resolution (where I just do the main effect without exiling myself again).\n\nFor tracking whether Paradigm has already been set up, I'm using a game registry that stores which cards have already triggered their exile-and-cast setup, so I only register the replacement effect and recurring trigger once. The key insight is that since replacement effects are applied after the card resolves, I can register the exile replacement inside the resolution handler and it'll intercept the card's movement from stack to graveyard.\n\nFor the library exile mechanic, I need to exile cards one at a time until the total converted mana cost reaches 4, accounting for the possibility of running out of library cards. Non-castable cards like lands stay exiled, and the player gets to choose which exiled cards they want to cast for free.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":700,"cache_read_input_tokens":90809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":700},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"2bb4102a-48d1-4ea0-855f-9f75d25a77e4","request_id":"req_011CbwHWcyaVfC7QGuPQ6XiJ"}
