{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_019mq2hDK6pzdxxTSrk768qf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! When a turn ends (wrap-around in `advance_phase`), the next player becomes active. I need to add skip_turns support here. When a player would become active, check if they have `skip_turns > 0`. If so, skip their turn and pass to the next player.\n\nBut this is a recursive problem - if I skip, I need to advance to the NEXT player's turn. And the NEXT player might also have `skip_turns > 0`. \n\nThe simplest implementation: in the \"End of turn — wrap around\" section, check if the new `active_player_index` player has `skip_turns > 0`. If so, decrement it and advance to the next player instead.\nLooking at how `extra_turns` works, I can see the pattern - it checks if there are extra turns queued and uses those, otherwise it cycles to the normal next player. I can integrate skip_turns logic right there: when determining the next active player, first check if they have skip_turns pending, and if so, decrement it and move to the following player instead.\n\nThe tricky part is handling this without assuming a 2-player game and avoiding infinite loops if multiple players have skip_turns active. I should keep it simple and just check once rather than looping through all possibilities.\n\nFor the implementation, I'll modify the `advance_phase` method to check if the newly active player has skip_turns remaining, and if so, decrement it and move to the next player. This keeps the change minimal and localized to where turns are actually being set up.\n\nWriting the full sos_97 implementation...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":132290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo"