{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01AaMMv9jRCQJekyZUCu3h44","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that existing tests don't seem to directly test loyalty ability activation. They test `on_resolve` directly. For the loyalty abilities in sos_97, since they're enclosed in `LoyaltyAbility` objects, I'll test them by:\n\n1. Creating the card\n2. Getting the loyalty abilities\n3. Calling the `LoyaltyAbilityInstance` with the proper setup\n\nLooking at how loyalty abilities work in the engine:\n- `LoyaltyAbility` has `loyalty_cost` and `effect`\n- `activate_ability(game, player, LoyaltyAbilityInstance(...))` adjusts loyalty and pushes to stack\n- When resolved, the effect function is called, which reads `pw.chosen_targets` to find targets\n\nFor the −1 ability that discards, targets are players chosen before activation, so I can set `pw.chosen_targets = [player]` directly before calling the effect. The −2 ability reanimates a creature from the graveyard, and I'll handle its targets the same way. Rather than going through the full loyalty activation pipeline, I'll test by creating the planeswalker and calling the ability effects directly.\n\nNow I'm setting up the tests for the dn_215 planeswalker's loyalty abilities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":960,"cache_read_input_tokens":140839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":960},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e9c65f7-ddbe-4353-b4d6-7512c729a9ad","uuid":"2024feda-99c3-45c1-857b-922d45ae62ff","request_id":"req_011CbwJGd6kEiS2XNhBkoJbE"}
